 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Every address a program uses is a lie. It is a virtual address, and the hardware translates it, on every single load and store. This video shows how, and how the TLB makes it fast."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Virtual memory and the TLB"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the eight stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why we want it, how pages and page tables work, and a translation done by hand."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then the TLB, the effective access time, protection, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: why virtual memory?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: why virtual memory"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each program gets its own address space starting at 0, as if it owned the whole machine. The compiler and linker never need to know where it will really sit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Protection: one process simply has no address that reaches another's memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Programs can be bigger than RAM. Pages not in use wait on disk, and are loaded only when touched."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And any page can go into any free frame, so loading is easy, and two processes can share a frame, like a shared library."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "main memory acts as a cache for the disk"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pages",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: memory is split into fixed-size pages, typically 4 kilobytes. Physical memory is split into frames of the same size."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: pages and the page table"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "va"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A 32-bit virtual address splits in two. The low 12 bits are the offset inside the page, because 2 to the 12 is 4096."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "va",
       "id": "o1",
       "lane": "virtual address",
       "start": 0,
       "end": 12,
       "label": "offset: bits 11 to 0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The top 20 bits are the virtual page number, the VPN."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "va",
       "id": "v1",
       "lane": "virtual address",
       "start": 12,
       "end": 32,
       "label": "VPN: bits 31 to 12 (20 bits)"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Translation replaces the VPN with a physical frame number, the PFN. The offset is copied unchanged."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "va",
       "id": "o2",
       "lane": "physical address",
       "start": 0,
       "end": 12,
       "label": "offset: copied"
      },
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "va",
       "id": "p2",
       "lane": "physical address",
       "start": 12,
       "end": 32,
       "label": "PFN: from the page table",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The page table holds one entry per virtual page. 20 bits of VPN means 2 to the 20 entries, about a million. At 4 bytes each, 4 megabytes, for every process."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "va"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ptm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ptm[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "ptm[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ptm[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "What is in an entry? First, the frame number."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ptm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pte"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pte[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A valid bit. If it is 0, the page is on disk, and touching it causes a page fault."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pte[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A dirty bit, set on a write, so the OS knows the page must be saved before it is evicted. Virtual memory is always write-back."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pte[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A reference bit, that the OS clears and checks to approximate LRU. And protection bits."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pte[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pte[4]",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "page table entry: PFN, valid, dirty, reference, protection"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "translate",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: a translation by hand. The program loads from virtual address hex 0 0 4 0 3 A B C."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: translating an address"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pte"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tr"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pt"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tr[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The low 12 bits, three hex digits, are the offset: A B C."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tr[2][1]",
       "value": "0xABC"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tr[2]",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The rest is the VPN: hex 0 0 4 0 3."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tr[1][1]",
       "value": "0x00403"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tr[1]",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The hardware indexes the page table with the VPN. Entry 4 0 3 is valid, and holds frame hex 1 F 2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pt[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tr[3][1]",
       "value": "0x1F2",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Put the frame number in front of the unchanged offset: hex 1 F 2 A B C. That is the physical address sent to the cache."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tr[4][1]",
       "value": "0x1F2ABC"
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "tr[4]",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Had the program touched page 4 0 2, the valid bit would be 0: a page fault. The OS loads the page from disk, updates the entry, and restarts the instruction."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pt[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "physical address = PFN followed by the same offset"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "multilevel",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: 4 megabytes per process is too much, and a 64-bit address would need far more. The fix is a multilevel page table."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 8: multilevel page tables"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "tr"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pt"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ml"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "x86-64 uses 48-bit virtual addresses and four levels. Each level uses 9 bits, picking one of 512 entries."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ml[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Level 1 points to a level 2 table, which points to level 3, then level 4, whose entry holds the frame number."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ml[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ml[1]",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ml[2]",
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ml[3]",
       "delay": 0.75
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The low 12 bits stay the offset. 9 times 4 plus 12 is 48."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ml[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "mlm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mlm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The win: tables are created only for the parts of the address space a program uses. A small program needs a handful of 4 kilobyte tables, not megabytes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "ml[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The cost: one translation now takes 4 memory reads, a page walk, before the real access. Without help, every load would be five times slower."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "multilevel: small tables, but a 4-read page walk"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tlb",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: the help is the TLB, the translation lookaside buffer. It is a small cache that holds recent translations."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 8: the TLB"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ml"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "mlm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tlb"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tlbx"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each entry holds a VPN as its tag, the frame number, and the valid, dirty and protection bits copied from the page table."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tlb[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Lookup VPN hex 0 0 4 0 3. All entries are compared at once. Entry 2 matches: a TLB hit, and the frame number comes out within the cycle."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tlbx[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tlb[1]",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tlbx[0][1]",
       "value": "hit: PFN 0x1F2",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Lookup VPN hex 0 0 4 0 4. No entry matches: a TLB miss."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tlbx[1]"
      },
      {
